;; Package poly1305 implements Poly1305 one-time message authentication code as
;; specified in https://cr.yp.to/mac/poly1305-20050329.pdf.
;;
;; Poly1305 is a fast, one-time authentication function. It is infeasible for an
;; attacker to generate an authenticator for a message without the key. However, a
;; key must only be used for a single message. Authenticating two different
;; messages with the same key allows an attacker to forge authenticators for other
;; messages with the same key.
;;
;; Poly1305 was originally coupled with AES in order to make Poly1305-AES. AES was
;; used with a fixed key in order to generate one-time keys from an nonce.
;; However, in this package AES isn't used and the one-time key is specified
;; directly.
(in-ns 'go.arbace.pytls.internal.poly1305) ^{:go/comments [[1 1 "// Copyright 2012 The Go Authors. All rights reserved."] [2 1 "// Use of this source code is governed by a BSD-style"] [3 1 "// license that can be found in the LICENSE file."] [5 1 "// Package poly1305 implements Poly1305 one-time message authentication code as"] [6 1 "// specified in https://cr.yp.to/mac/poly1305-20050329.pdf."] [7 1 "//"] [8 1 "// Poly1305 is a fast, one-time authentication function. It is infeasible for an"] [9 1 "// attacker to generate an authenticator for a message without the key. However, a"] [10 1 "// key must only be used for a single message. Authenticating two different"] [11 1 "// messages with the same key allows an attacker to forge authenticators for other"] [12 1 "// messages with the same key."] [13 1 "//"] [14 1 "// Poly1305 was originally coupled with AES in order to make Poly1305-AES. AES was"] [15 1 "// used with a fixed key in order to generate one-time keys from an nonce."] [16 1 "// However, in this package AES isn't used and the one-time key is specified"] [17 1 "// directly."] [22 1 "// TagSize is the size, in bytes, of a poly1305 authenticator."] [25 1 "// Sum generates an authenticator for msg using a one-time key and puts the"] [26 1 "// 16-byte result into out. Authenticating two different messages with the same"] [27 1 "// key allows an attacker to forge messages at will."] [34 1 "// Verify returns true if mac is a valid authenticator for m with the given key."] [41 1 "// New returns a new MAC computing an authentication"] [42 1 "// tag of all data written to it with the given key."] [43 1 "// This allows writing the message progressively instead"] [44 1 "// of passing it as a single slice. Common users should use"] [45 1 "// the Sum function instead."] [46 1 "//"] [47 1 "// The key must be unique for each message, as authenticating"] [48 1 "// two different messages with the same key allows an attacker"] [49 1 "// to forge messages at will."] [56 1 "// MAC is an io.Writer computing an authentication tag"] [57 1 "// of the data written to it."] [58 1 "//"] [59 1 "// MAC cannot be used like common hash.Hash implementations,"] [60 1 "// because using a poly1305 key twice breaks its security."] [61 1 "// Therefore writing data to a running MAC after calling"] [62 1 "// Sum or Verify causes it to panic."] [64 6 "// platform-dependent implementation"] [69 1 "// Size returns the number of bytes Sum will return."] [72 1 "// Write adds more data to the running message authentication code."] [73 1 "// It never returns an error."] [74 1 "//"] [75 1 "// It must not be called after the first call of Sum or Verify."] [83 1 "// Sum computes the authenticator of all data written to the"] [84 1 "// message authentication code."] [92 1 "// Verify returns whether the authenticator of all data written to"] [93 1 "// the message authentication code matches the expected value."]] :go/pos {:name [18 9] :package [18 1]} :go/semis []} (go/file "poly1305.go" :doc "Package poly1305 implements Poly1305 one-time message authentication code as\nspecified in https://cr.yp.to/mac/poly1305-20050329.pdf.\n\nPoly1305 is a fast, one-time authentication function. It is infeasible for an\nattacker to generate an authenticator for a message without the key. However, a\nkey must only be used for a single message. Authenticating two different\nmessages with the same key allows an attacker to forge authenticators for other\nmessages with the same key.\n\nPoly1305 was originally coupled with AES in order to make Poly1305-AES. AES was\nused with a fixed key in order to generate one-time keys from an nonce.\nHowever, in this package AES isn't used and the one-time key is specified\ndirectly.\n" :imports [

